---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import ToolVote from '../../../components/ToolVote.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Bordvakt"
  description="Some restaurants release a month of tables in one batch and lose them in minutes. This watches for the release and tells you what it opened. Working prototype."
>
  <main class="reading" id="main">
    <section class="block insight-page">
      <p class="kicker"><a href="/tools/">Tools</a></p>
      <h1>Bordvakt</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        Some restaurants release a month of tables in one batch, and lose them in minutes. This one waits for
        the release so you do not have to.
      </p>

      <h2>What it tries to solve</h2>

      <p>
        The good sittings exist for about as long as it takes to read the page they appeared on. What is left
        an hour later is the late tables nobody wanted — so the useful question is not "is there a table
        tonight" but what the next release will open, and whether it contains a night you want. The
        alternative is refreshing a booking page for a month, which is not a plan so much as a hobby.
      </p>

      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li>
          <strong>It explains a nothing.</strong> "0 matches" reads like a full restaurant, when the usual
          cause is that the times on offer fall outside the window you asked for. So it says which:
          <em>13 on offer but none between 18:00 and 20:00 — they sit at 21:00, 21:30.</em>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Preferences rank, they never exclude.</strong> An ideal night decides which of several
          acceptable tables is offered first. It never rules one out.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Nothing is booked without you.</strong> An alert is an alert; the booking waits for a
          button, and changing that takes a deliberate trip into settings.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The walkthrough</h2>

      <p>
        Ten frames from the running prototype, on one Mac watching three Stockholm restaurants that all book
        through the same engine. The numbers in the screens came back from real sweeps.
      </p>

      <p>
        And it is not only a recording. Switch to <em>try it yourself</em> and the window takes the full width
        of the page, running the real matching logic over a snapshot of what was actually free: change the
        evenings, move the window, exclude a week, and what appears, how it ranks and the sentence explaining
        a miss are all recomputed the way the watcher computes them. Two honest limits — the availability is
        frozen at the moment the page was built, and the booking button only pretends.
      </p>

      <p class="demo-open">
        <a class="demo-button" href="/tools/bordvakt-demo.html?mode=try">Open the clickable prototype →</a>
        <span class="demo-hint">It is an application. A big screen suits it.</span>
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="demo-wide">
      <iframe
        id="bordvakt-demo"
        src="/tools/bordvakt-demo.html"
        title="Bordvakt walkthrough"
        loading="lazy"
        scrolling="no"
      ></iframe>
      <p class="demo-fallback">
        <a href="/tools/bordvakt-demo.html">Open the walkthrough on its own</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="block insight-page">
      <ToolVote tool="bordvakt" />
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .insight-page h2 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin: 2.6rem 0 0.7rem;
  }
  .feature-list {
    margin: 1.4rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }
  .feature-list li {
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .feature-list strong {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  /* The walkthrough is wider than the reading measure, so it steps out of the
     column to the shell width the rest of the site uses. */
  .demo-wide {
    width: min(65rem, calc(100vw - 3rem));
    margin: 2rem 0 3.4rem 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
  }
  /* On a phone the reading gutter is worth more to the walkthrough than to the
     margin: the device mock has a floor it cannot shrink past. */
  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .demo-wide {
      width: 100vw;
    }
  }
  .demo-wide iframe {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 1400px;
    border: 0;
  }
  .demo-open {
    margin: 1.6rem 0 0;
  }
  .demo-hint {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-left: 0.8rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--bark);
  }
  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .demo-hint {
      display: block;
      margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    }
  }
  .demo-button {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--moss);
    border-radius: 2px;
    font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--moss);
    transition: background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .demo-button:hover {
    background: var(--moss);
    color: var(--paper);
  }
  .demo-fallback {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
    font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Same-origin, so the height can be measured directly rather than posted
  // across, and the site's theme toggle can be handed through to the frame.
  const frame = document.getElementById('bordvakt-demo') as HTMLIFrameElement | null;

  if (frame) {
    const syncTheme = () => {
      const doc = frame.contentDocument;
      if (!doc) return;
      const theme = document.documentElement.dataset.theme;
      if (theme) doc.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
      else delete doc.documentElement.dataset.theme;
    };

    const syncHeight = () => {
      const doc = frame.contentDocument;
      if (!doc?.body) return;
      frame.style.height = `${doc.body.scrollHeight + 8}px`;
    };

    const wire = () => {
      syncTheme();
      syncHeight();
      const doc = frame.contentDocument;
      if (doc?.body && 'ResizeObserver' in window) {
        new ResizeObserver(syncHeight).observe(doc.body);
      }
      // The walkthrough advances on its own, and each frame is a different height.
      setInterval(syncHeight, 1000);
    };

    frame.addEventListener('load', wire);
    // A lazy frame can finish before this script runs, in which case the load
    // event has already been and gone.
    if (frame.contentDocument?.readyState === 'complete') wire();

    new MutationObserver(syncTheme).observe(document.documentElement, {
      attributes: true,
      attributeFilter: ['data-theme'],
    });
  }
</script>
